        "prefix_token_count": 49,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Let \\( d = \\gcd(n + 7, 2n + 1) \\). By definition, \\( d \\) divides both \\( n + 7 \\) and \\( 2n + 1 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 216,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 218,
        "char_start": 110,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 86,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 87,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Since \\( d \\) divides \\( n + 7 \\), we can express this as \\( n + 7 = kd \\) for some integer \\( k \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 339,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 341,
        "char_start": 220,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 130,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 131,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Similarly, since \\( d \\) divides \\( 2n + 1 \\), we can express this as \\( 2n + 1 = ld \\) for some integer \\( l \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 467,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 469,
        "char_start": 343,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 169,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 170,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: We can eliminate \\( n \\) by manipulating these equations. Multiply the first equation by 2 to get \\( 2n + 14 = 2kd \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 590,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 592,
        "char_start": 471,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 214,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 215,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Subtract the second equation from this new equation to eliminate \\( 2n \\): \\( (2n + 14) - (2n + 1) = 2kd - ld \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 645,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 647,
        "char_start": 594,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 237,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 238,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Simplify the left side: \\( 13 = (2k - l)d \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 728,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 729,
        "char_start": 649,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 269,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 270,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: This shows that \\( d \\) must divide 13. The divisors of 13 are 1 and 13."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 877,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 878,
        "char_start": 731,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 323,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 324,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: To determine if \\( d = 13 \\) is possible, check if there exists an \\( n \\) such that both \\( n + 7 \\) and \\( 2n + 1 \\) are multiples of 13."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 957,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 959,
        "char_start": 880,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 360,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 361,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Set \\( n + 7 = 13m \\) for some integer \\( m \\). Then \\( n = 13m - 7 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1063,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1065,
        "char_start": 961,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 425,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 426,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: Substitute \\( n = 13m - 7 \\) into \\( 2n + 1 \\): \\( 2(13m - 7) + 1 = 26m - 14 + 1 = 26m - 13 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1150,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1151,
        "char_start": 1067,
        "effective_step": 11,
        "end_token_index": 464,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 465,
        "step_number": 11,
        "text": "Step 11: Notice that \\( 26m - 13 = 13(2m - 1) \\), which is clearly a multiple of 13."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1204,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
